---
import ExternalLink from "@src/components/actions/external-link/ExternalLink.astro";
import Container from "@src/components/layout/container/Container.astro";
import Section from "@src/components/layout/section/Section.astro";
import Eyebrow from "@src/components/typography/eyebrow/Eyebrow.astro";
import Prose from "@src/components/typography/prose/Prose.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import {siteConfig} from "@src/site/SiteConfig";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Neil Armstrong"
  description="What this website does and does not do with visitor data: no cookies, no analytics, an optional map request, and a contact form."
>
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <Prose>
        <Eyebrow>Privacy</Eyebrow>

        <h1>Privacy</h1>

        <p>
          This site doesn’t use cookies, analytics, advertising, tracking pixels, or embedded social content, and it has
          no accounts. The only personal data I receive is what you choose to send through the contact form.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>

        <p>
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical data such as your IP address and browser details
          when you request a page. That is covered by
          <ExternalLink href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
            GitHub’s privacy statement
          </ExternalLink>
          , and I don’t have access to those logs.
        </p>

        <h2>Ride maps</h2>

        <p>
          Cycling ride logs can show a map. Nothing is requested for it until you open a ride log and scroll the map
          into view. It then loads map tiles from OpenStreetMap, which means your IP address and browser details are
          sent to the OpenStreetMap Foundation. See the
          <ExternalLink href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy">OpenStreetMap privacy policy</ExternalLink>
          . If you don’t open a ride log, the request is never made.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact form</h2>

        <p>
          If you use the contact form, your name, email address, and message are sent to a Cloudflare Worker, which
          emails them to me. I use them only to reply, and the Worker doesn’t store them. The form uses Cloudflare
          Turnstile to tell people from bots, which runs in your browser and may send Cloudflare technical data such as
          your IP address. See
          <ExternalLink href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</ExternalLink>.
        </p>

        <h2>Links elsewhere</h2>

        <p>
          Links to LinkedIn, GitHub, Strava, Instagram, and other sites take you to services with their own privacy
          practices.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          For any privacy question, message me on
          <ExternalLink href={siteConfig.socialLinks.linkedIn.href}>LinkedIn</ExternalLink>.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
